{"data": [{"author_id": "2044006204226113536", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:01:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116183618179543142"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 152, "start": 148, "tag": "LLM"}, {"end": 156, "start": 153, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 173, "start": 157, "tag": "MachineLearning"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "awesomepapers.io/llm-papers/pap…", "end": 147, "expanded_url": "https://awesomepapers.io/llm-papers/papers/2608.21867?utm_source=social&utm_medium=x&utm_campaign=sota", "start": 124, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://awesomepapers.io/llm-papers/papers/2608.21867?utm_source=social&utm_medium=x&utm_campaign=sota", "url": "https://t.co/f3Mh4n58jm"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/zJfnGaZ0rA", "end": 197, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/awesomepapersio/status/2116183618179543142/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116183616833105920", "start": 174, "url": "https://t.co/zJfnGaZ0rA"}]}, "id": "2116183618179543142", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "⚡ NEW SOTA · SWE-bench Verified\n\nMemGuard: Persisting Verifier Signals for LLM-Agent Memory Governance\n83.6%\n↑ from 239%\n\n🔗 https://t.co/f3Mh4n58jm\n#LLM #AI #MachineLearning https://t.co/zJfnGaZ0rA", "url": "https://x.com/awesomepapersio/status/2116183618179543142"}, {"author_id": "1923609574210191360", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:59:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116198370230550886"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/32rDgaEn8I", "end": 251, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116198370230550886/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116197170961608704", "start": 228, "url": "https://t.co/32rDgaEn8I"}]}, "id": "2116198370230550886", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "1/ Benchmark Teardown #3: Cost per successful task\n\nI compared 19 agent configurations on the same 45 SWE-bench Verified tasks.\n\nThe results raise an interesting question: are expensive coding agents actually worth the premium? https://t.co/32rDgaEn8I", "url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116198370230550886"}, {"author_id": "1896345067108851712", "created_at": "2026-10-29T22:32:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115934708668506199"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "How to negotiate an AI agent benchmark pricing clause tying vendor price hikes to independently verified benchmark gains, not marketing claims.", "display_url": "startupfortune.com/how-to-negotia…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://startupfortune.com/how-to-negotiate-an-ai-agent-benchmark-pricing-clause/", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115934754851938304/FomxZI3q?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115934754851938304/FomxZI3q?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 243, "status": 200, "title": "How To Negotiate An AI Agent Benchmark Pricing Clause - Startup Fortune", "unwound_url": "https://startupfortune.com/how-to-negotiate-an-ai-agent-benchmark-pricing-clause/", "url": "https://t.co/R0U8AocWU4"}]}, "id": "2115934708668506199", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 26, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "An AI agent benchmark pricing clause ties price hikes to independently verified gains, not vendor marketing. Buyers are pushing it into renewals now, naming benchmarks like SWE-bench and labs like Epoch AI to check claims before paying more.\n\nhttps://t.co/R0U8AocWU4", "url": "https://x.com/Startup_Fortune/status/2115934708668506199"}, {"author_id": "894631624809345024", "created_at": "2026-10-31T12:09:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116502941607858485"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/krD2Rua8ej", "end": 233, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/nemui_nekoooo/status/2116502941607858485/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116502933609299968", "start": 210, "url": "https://t.co/krD2Rua8ej"}]}, "id": "2116502941607858485", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 321, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI's hardest tests don't last long:\n\nHumanity's Last Exam: 9% → 61% in 21 months ARC-AGI-2: 3% → 95% in 19 months ARC-AGI-3: 0.4% → 63% in 6 months\n\nEvery new \"impossible\" benchmark falls faster than the last. https://t.co/krD2Rua8ej", "url": "https://x.com/nemui_nekoooo/status/2116502941607858485"}, {"author_id": "1923609574210191360", "created_at": "2026-10-31T16:06:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116562354196681093"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Mhbhzrt86d", "end": 249, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116562354196681093/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116561871629086720", "start": 226, "url": "https://t.co/Mhbhzrt86d"}]}, "id": "2116562354196681093", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Benchmark Teardown #4: Where did the money go?\n\nI analyzed 855 coding-agent runs on SWE-bench Verified: 19 model + agent configurations, 45 shared tasks, one run each, and $1,449 in logged spend.\n\nHere’s where the runs went 👇 https://t.co/Mhbhzrt86d", "url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116562354196681093"}, {"author_id": "2109046651298205696", "created_at": "2026-10-31T15:54:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116559545233441062"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 220, "id": "1714438092655149056", "start": 212, "username": "ChatGPT"}, {"end": 241, "id": "84107004", "start": 234, "username": "Claude"}, {"end": 265, "id": "1720665183188922368", "start": 260, "username": "grok"}]}, "id": "2116559545233441062", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Happy Halloween, fellow sci-fi enthusiasts! 🎃\n\nHere’s a scary question: who’s closest to AGI: artificial general intelligence: GPT, Claude, or Grok?\n\nBest reported scores on the ARC-AGI-2 reasoning benchmark:\n\n• @ChatGPT Astra: 95%\n• @Claude Opus 5.5: 93.3%\n• @Grok 4.7: 61.4%", "url": "https://x.com/AshMaddoxWrites/status/2116559545233441062"}, {"author_id": "266259493", "created_at": "2026-10-30T03:52:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116015234930606201"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/cognition/stat…", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cognition/status/2115983299432820864", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/XknH76ksLb"}]}, "id": "2116015234930606201", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 104, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115983299432820864", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Cognition's leaderboard says Claude Opus 5.5 tops its FrontierCode 2.0 benchmark at 45.5%. Read that twice. The best model in the world still merges clean on less than half of real pull requests, by the standard of a maintainer who has to live with the code afterward. https://t.co/XknH76ksLb", "url": "https://x.com/stretchcloud/status/2116015234930606201"}, {"author_id": "1888243667804241920", "created_at": "2026-10-30T01:46:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115983602228043903"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 7, "start": 0, "tag": "keepo1"}, {"end": 19, "start": 9, "tag": "ChatGPTo1"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/dCK91Vqgsh", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GuaiMie77/status/2115983602228043903/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115983530832596992", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/dCK91Vqgsh"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/dCK91Vqgsh", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GuaiMie77/status/2115983602228043903/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115983543587438592", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/dCK91Vqgsh"}]}, "id": "2115983602228043903", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 338, "like_count": 28, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "#keepo1  #ChatGPTo1\n\nAnother reason to preserve o1: its software-engineering capabilities.\n\nOpenAI reported a score of 48.9% on SWE-bench Verified for o1-2024-12-17.\n\nThis benchmark evaluates resolving real software issues using a repository and an issue description. It tests an https://t.co/dCK91Vqgsh", "url": "https://x.com/GuaiMie77/status/2115983602228043903"}, {"author_id": "1993062696028438528", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:26:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116204986304811458"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 185, "id": "13334762", "start": 178, "username": "github"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/17434878649341…", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/1743487864934162432/status/2115477376981508419", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/sZ93r9F40b"}]}, "id": "2116204986304811458", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 70, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115477376981508419", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Copilot Fusion came within two benchmark points of Claude Code at roughly half the API cost per task in Artificial Analysis’s test.\n\nCopilot Fusion is now generally available in @github Copilot. It isn't a new model. It picks Anthropic or OpenAI models for each task, and on https://t.co/sZ93r9F40b", "url": "https://x.com/koltregaskes2/status/2116204986304811458"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "created_at": "2026-10-29T23:08:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115943903874724206"], "id": "2115943903874724206", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 187, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "As of October 29, Vals AI has Claude Opus 5.5 in first place on its Terminal-Bench 4.0 leaderboard.\n\nTerminal-Bench 4.0 is a fresh set of 66 community-contributed tasks. None of them appear in Terminal-Bench 2.1. Each task is built around a real deliverable, such as a working", "url": "https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2115943903874724206"}, {"author_id": "2081100144708079616", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:31:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116206258487181395", "2116206350619554278"], "id": "2116206258487181395", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a quick timeline of what ai did in 2026 while everyone was busy arguing about which chatbot is smarter:\n\nmay: an openai model disproves an erdős conjecture\n\njuly: a claude model finds a counterexample to the jacobian conjecture, open for nearly 100 years\n\naugust: openai drops", "url": "https://x.com/itsallsi/status/2116206258487181395"}, {"author_id": "2081100144708079616", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:31:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116206258487181395", "2116206350619554278"], "id": "2116206350619554278", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 34, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a quick timeline of what AI/SI did in 2026 while everyone was busy arguing about which chatbot is smarter:\n\nmay: an openai model disproves an erdős conjecture\n\njuly: a claude model finds a counterexample to the jacobian conjecture, open for nearly 100 years\n\naugust: openai drops", "url": "https://x.com/itsallsi/status/2116206350619554278"}, {"author_id": "1960272689777737728", "created_at": "2026-10-30T04:15:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116021216993796189"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/N9YKt8OPh6", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/shvgroups/status/2116021216993796189/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116021156390260736", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/N9YKt8OPh6"}]}, "id": "2116021216993796189", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 348, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Today we share how fixed benchmark might not be the answer to judge rapidly growing AI agent and models.\n\nOpponents you can't memorise: a research note on how we evaluate AI agents\n\nIn short: fixed benchmarks lose accuracy once they are public, because test sets leak into https://t.co/N9YKt8OPh6", "url": "https://x.com/shvgroups/status/2116021216993796189"}, {"article": {"title": "Grok Bot Used to Have Its Own Meter. The X Subscription Ended That."}, "author_id": "2098059182444552192", "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:53:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116166677172019588"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2115…", "end": 91, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115702335817052160", "start": 68, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115702335817052160", "url": "https://t.co/epf6SYrFOx"}]}, "id": "2116166677172019588", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 736, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Grok Bot Used to Have Its Own Meter. The X Subscription Ended That. https://t.co/epf6SYrFOx", "url": "https://x.com/Maxrune/status/2116166677172019588"}, {"article": {"title": "The Slopsquatting Trap: How Autonomous Coding Agents Weaponize Phantom Dependencies"}, "author_id": "67694456", "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:15:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116625152721227845"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2116…", "end": 270, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116621558114643968", "start": 247, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116621558114643968", "url": "https://t.co/1i8tyP4ItU"}]}, "id": "2116625152721227845", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 113, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "LLMs hallucinate phantom packages in 18% of code.\n\nNow attackers pre-register those names on PyPI with malware. When your coding agent hits ModuleNotFoundError and runs `pip install`, you just gave them root.\n\nThe Slopsquatting Trap, and the fix: https://t.co/1i8tyP4ItU", "url": "https://x.com/PatchOnChain/status/2116625152721227845"}, {"article": {"title": "Intelligence That Compounds Through Experience"}, "author_id": "2040374346158682112", "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:52:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116619411453010303"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2116…", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116600330314297344", "start": 132, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116600330314297344", "url": "https://t.co/TY1Ng01ADs"}]}, "id": "2116619411453010303", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 128, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "The biggest opportunity I see in AI right now isn’t just scale. It’s building systems that can safely learn from what happens next. https://t.co/TY1Ng01ADs", "url": "https://x.com/Kev1nChang/status/2116619411453010303"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2044006204226113536", "name": "Awesome Papers", "username": "awesomepapersio"}, {"id": "1923609574210191360", "name": "Craig Michael Dsouza", "username": "CraigMLdsouza"}, {"id": "1896345067108851712", "name": "Startup Fortune", "username": "Startup_Fortune"}, {"id": "894631624809345024", "name": "Odd ☆☆", "username": "nemui_nekoooo"}, {"id": "2109046651298205696", "name": "Ash Maddox", "username": "AshMaddoxWrites"}, {"id": "266259493", "name": "Prasenjit Sarkar", "username": "stretchcloud"}, {"id": "1888243667804241920", "name": "乖小咩", "username": "GuaiMie77"}, {"id": "1993062696028438528", "name": "Kol Tregaskes News", "username": "koltregaskes2"}, {"id": "1165159200470650881", "name": "AI Quanting", "username": "AIQuanting"}, {"id": "208110014470807